description: Nitro API, transformers, and Telegram server rules
globs: server/**/*.{ts,js}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Server / API

- New routes: `server/api/{supabase|bgg|tesera|common}/name.get.ts` or `.post.ts` (`/api/supabase` prefix is historical).
- Domain DB: `#server/db` (Drizzle). Auth identity: `requireUser` / `serverSupabaseUser`. Storage uploads still use `#supabase/server`.
- Map DB ↔ UI in `server/transformers.ts`; do not scatter snake↔camel mapping in pages.
- Domain handlers: `throw createError({ statusCode, statusMessage })` on failure.
- BGG/Tesera proxies: keep returning soft errors (`{ items: [], error }`) unless changing intentionally.
- TG Login: verify with `checkTelegramAuth`; password via `telegram-password-generator`; profile upsert via `upsert-profile` into local Postgres. Prefer extending existing handlers over copying a fifth auth path.
- Notifications: `telegramNotify` / `sendTelegramMessage`; pgmq queue path exists but store is often commented — do not enable scheduled `telegram:send-messages` without ask.
- Bots under `server/telegram-bots/*` are standalone; starter plugin currently launches none.
- BGG rate limit plugin serializes `/api/bgg/*` — avoid bypassing it for new BGG calls.
